":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"props"},{"type":"text","value":" properties"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"props-property-children\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ComponentChildren"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The components to render — always rendered unconditionally, not gated on hydration. New queries are hydrated into the cache during render; for queries that already exist in the cache, only newer dehydrated data is hydrated, and that happens in an effect after commit, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":" may render briefly before it lands."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"props-property-options\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/OmitKeyof.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OmitKeyof"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/HydrateOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HydrateOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"defaultOptions\""},{"type":"text","value":"> & "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optional. Note: unlike "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hydrate"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mutations"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be set here."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"props-property-queryclient\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient?"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../classes/QueryClient.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use this to use a custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":". Otherwise, the one from the nearest context will be used."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"<a id=\"props-property-state\">"},{"type":"inlineHtml","value":"</a>"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/DehydratedState.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DehydratedState"}]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The state to hydrate."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Element"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The provided "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"children"},{"type":"text","value":", rendered unconditionally. New queries in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" are hydrated into the\ncache during render; for queries already in the cache, only newer dehydrated data is hydrated, in an effect\nafter commit."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { HydrationBoundary } from '@tanstack/preact-query'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedState}>...</HydrationBoundary>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-side prefetch handed off to the client via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dehydrate"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { HydrationBoundary, dehydrate, noop } from '@tanstack/preact-query'\n\nasync function ServerComponent() {\n  const queryClient = getQueryClient()\n\n  await queryClient\n    .query({\n      queryKey: ['posts'],\n      queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    })\n    .catch(noop)\n\n  return (\n    <HydrationBoundary state={dehydrate(queryClient)}>\n      <Posts />\n    </HydrationBoundary>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"props","text":"props","level":3},{"id":"props-properties","text":"props properties","level":4},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction HydrationBoundary(props: HydrationBoundaryProps): Element;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/preact-query/src/HydrationBoundary.tsx:86](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/preact-query/src/HydrationBoundary.tsx#L86)\n\n`HydrationBoundary` adds a previously dehydrated state into the `queryClient` that would be returned by\n`useQueryClient()`. If the client already contains data, the new queries will be intelligently merged based on\nupdate timestamp.\n\nNote: Only `queries` can be dehydrated with an `HydrationBoundary`.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### props\n\n[`HydrationBoundaryProps`](../interfaces/HydrationBoundaryProps.md)\n\nThe dehydrated `state` to hydrate, the hydrate `options`, an optional custom\n`queryClient`, and the `children` to render.\n\n<a id=\"props-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `props` properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"props-property-children\"></a> `children?` | `ComponentChildren` | The components to render — always rendered unconditionally, not gated on hydration. New queries are hydrated into the cache during render; for queries that already exist in the cache, only newer dehydrated data is hydrated, and that happens in an effect after commit, so `children` may render briefly before it lands. |\n| <a id=\"props-property-options\"></a> `options?` | [`OmitKeyof`](../type-aliases/OmitKeyof.md)\\<[`HydrateOptions`](../interfaces/HydrateOptions.md), `\"defaultOptions\"`\\> & `object` | Optional. Note: unlike `hydrate`, `mutations` cannot be set here. |\n| <a id=\"props-property-queryclient\"></a> `queryClient?` | [`QueryClient`](../classes/QueryClient.md) | Use this to use a custom `QueryClient`. Otherwise, the one from the nearest context will be used. |\n| <a id=\"props-property-state\"></a> `state` | [`DehydratedState`](../interfaces/DehydratedState.md) \\| `null` \\| `undefined` | The state to hydrate. |\n\n## Returns\n\n`Element`\n\nThe provided `children`, rendered unconditionally. New queries in `state` are hydrated into the\ncache during render; for queries already in the cache, only newer dehydrated data is hydrated, in an effect\nafter commit.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { HydrationBoundary } from '@tanstack/preact-query'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedState}>...</HydrationBoundary>\n}\n```\n\nServer-side prefetch handed off to the client via `dehydrate`:\n```tsx\nimport { HydrationBoundary, dehydrate, noop } from '@tanstack/preact-query'\n\nasync function ServerComponent() {\n  const queryClient = getQueryClient()\n\n  await queryClient\n    .query({\n      queryKey: ['posts'],\n      queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    })\n    .catch(noop)\n\n  return (\n    <HydrationBoundary state={dehydrate(queryClient)}>\n      <Posts />\n    </HydrationBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: HydrationBoundary\ntitle: HydrationBoundary\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction HydrationBoundary(props: HydrationBoundaryProps): Element;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/preact-query/src/HydrationBoundary.tsx:86](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/packages/preact-query/src/HydrationBoundary.tsx#L86)\n\n`HydrationBoundary` adds a previously dehydrated state into the `queryClient` that would be returned by\n`useQueryClient()`. If the client already contains data, the new queries will be intelligently merged based on\nupdate timestamp.\n\nNote: Only `queries` can be dehydrated with an `HydrationBoundary`.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### props\n\n[`HydrationBoundaryProps`](../interfaces/HydrationBoundaryProps.md)\n\nThe dehydrated `state` to hydrate, the hydrate `options`, an optional custom\n`queryClient`, and the `children` to render.\n\n<a id=\"props-properties\"></a>\n\n#### `props` properties\n\n| Property | Type | Description |\n| ------ | ------ | ------ |\n| <a id=\"props-property-children\"></a> `children?` | `ComponentChildren` | The components to render — always rendered unconditionally, not gated on hydration. New queries are hydrated into the cache during render; for queries that already exist in the cache, only newer dehydrated data is hydrated, and that happens in an effect after commit, so `children` may render briefly before it lands. |\n| <a id=\"props-property-options\"></a> `options?` | [`OmitKeyof`](../type-aliases/OmitKeyof.md)\\<[`HydrateOptions`](../interfaces/HydrateOptions.md), `\"defaultOptions\"`\\> & `object` | Optional. Note: unlike `hydrate`, `mutations` cannot be set here. |\n| <a id=\"props-property-queryclient\"></a> `queryClient?` | [`QueryClient`](../classes/QueryClient.md) | Use this to use a custom `QueryClient`. Otherwise, the one from the nearest context will be used. |\n| <a id=\"props-property-state\"></a> `state` | [`DehydratedState`](../interfaces/DehydratedState.md) \\| `null` \\| `undefined` | The state to hydrate. |\n\n## Returns\n\n`Element`\n\nThe provided `children`, rendered unconditionally. New queries in `state` are hydrated into the\ncache during render; for queries already in the cache, only newer dehydrated data is hydrated, in an effect\nafter commit.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { HydrationBoundary } from '@tanstack/preact-query'\n\nfunction App() {\n  return <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedState}>...</HydrationBoundary>\n}\n```\n\nServer-side prefetch handed off to the client via `dehydrate`:\n```tsx\nimport { HydrationBoundary, dehydrate, noop } from '@tanstack/preact-query'\n\nasync function ServerComponent() {\n  const queryClient = getQueryClient()\n\n  await queryClient\n    .query({\n      queryKey: ['posts'],\n      queryFn: fetchPosts,\n    })\n    .catch(noop)\n\n  return (\n    <HydrationBoundary state={dehydrate(queryClient)}>\n      <Posts />\n    </HydrationBoundary>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
